   Regarding my choice of "I**2" as the subject line header for
this thread:  I picked it up from Dr. Timothy Leary's "SMILE" acronym,
where he squares the "I".  His acronym stands for "Space Migration,
Intelligence Increase, Life Extension".  I liked "I**2" because of
the allusion to Leary and the fact that it is only 4 characters long.
Of course, others are free to coin a more appropriate header.

   Regarding the "legitimacy" of this thread:  One or more posters
have stated or implied that one's innate intelligence cannot be 
changed.  I would accept this as a null hypothesis to be tested, but
not as an eternal verity.  In the spirit of "dynamic optimism" and
"boundless expansion", I think it's at least worth a look.  If it is
indeed possible to increase one's intelligence, that would certainly
be "extropic", would it not?


References:
-----------
   Since at least two extropians have asked, here is the Ertl reference:

   Ertl, John P. "Evoked Potentials and Intelligence."  Lecture
delivered by the Director of Cybernetic Studies at University of
Ottawa, March 30, 1967, reprinted under the title "Intelligence
Testing by Brainwaves."  MENSA Bulletin. CX, April, 1968.
(note -- I got this reference from the book "How to Increase Your
Intelligence" by Win Wenger, Ph.D., copyright 1975.  Also, I must
confess that I haven't read the article, I merely discussed the
idea with Dr. Wenger on the phone)

